IBM Bob was used as an AI-assisted development partner for the Skin Lesion Classification project.

It supported the team in understanding and organizing the machine-learning workflow,
including dataset preparation, image preprocessing, ResNet50 transfer learning, training,
fine-tuning, evaluation, and documentation. IBM Bob also helped explain code, identify
issues in the notebook workflow, improve code readability, and interpret performance metrics
such as accuracy, ROC-AUC, precision, recall, F1 score, specificity, and the confusion matrix.

The project uses Python, PyTorch, Torchvision, Pandas, Scikit-learn, and Jupyter Notebook.
The model classifies dermoscopic skin-lesion images as benign or malignant using the ISIC 2019 dataset.
IBM Bob helped the team work more efficiently, document technical decisions, and maintain a
structured end-to-end development process.
